# The live-quiz image needs labs/ (worksheets) AND slides/ (lecture decks), which
# are siblings, so the build context is the repo root.
#
# That makes THIS FILE the boundary. It is an allowlist — deny everything, then
# re-admit exactly what the image needs — because a denylist here fails open:
# forgetting one entry ships it. `instructor/` holds every answer key, exam key
# and research instrument, is git-ignored, and is present on disk during a build.
# It must never enter the context.
*
!labs/
!slides/

# …and within those, nothing generated or private.
labs/**/.venv
labs/**/__pycache__
labs/**/.pytest_cache
labs/**/*.pyc
labs/**/node_modules
labs/live-quiz/*.db
# Student uploads belong on the /data volume, never in the image. This directory is where a
# local run (or a stray test) drops them, and it is baked in TWICE (COPY labs/live-quiz/ and
# COPY labs/). Git-ignored, so only an in-place build from a working tree can pick it up; the
# 2026-10-09 production image shipped with a leftover file from here. The app creates its
# upload dir itself (os.makedirs in submission.py), so excluding it breaks nothing.
labs/live-quiz/uploads
labs/week11-memory-safety-exploitation/vuln
labs/week11-memory-safety-exploitation/vuln-*
labs/week11-memory-safety-exploitation/fuzz
slides/pptx
